## Challengers after v0.1.0

Registered in two addenda before any challenger score existed: evaluation/plan_v2.yaml (the graph
features) and evaluation/plan_v3.yaml (a sequence model). Each challenger is trained on its champion's
rows and sample, graded on the same test months with the same code, and replaces a champion only
with an interval of the difference clear of zero and above it.

{{ table("v2.challengers") }}
{% if has("v2.payments.lightgbm_graph.capture.estimate") %}

On payments the graph challenger cleared every gate and still captured less than the champion,
{{ v("v2.payments.lightgbm_graph.capture.estimate") }} of fraud dollars against
{{ v("eval.payments.lightgbm.capture_usd.estimate") }}, so the champion stays. The ablation with
only the structure of the merchant graph, without the counts of fraud already known, captured
{{ v("v2.payments.lightgbm_structure.capture.estimate") }}. That points at the known fraud counts as
what pulled the challenger down, but the addendum registered no test of it, so it is a lead and not
a finding. The ablation sits outside the registered family, so it has no comparison with the floor
and that gate reads as failed; its declines were also over the limit of the budget. On logins the
graph features took the model from {{ v("eval.logins.lightgbm.capture.estimate") }} to
{{ v("v2.logins.lightgbm_graph.capture.estimate") }}, still short of the rules floor at
{{ v("eval.logins.floor.capture.estimate") }}, so that desk stays on its floor.
{% endif %}
{% if has("v2.payments.gru.capture.estimate") %}

The sequence challenger reads each card's earlier events as well as this one. It cleared every gate
and captured {{ v("v2.payments.gru.capture.estimate") }} of fraud dollars against the champion's
{{ v("eval.payments.lightgbm.capture_usd.estimate") }}, with the interval of the difference clear of
zero, so the registered rule promotes it. Its first grade failed
the calibration gate with no value at all, because the grader knew probabilities by model name only;
the grader now reads the logistic output the addendum registered, the bound unchanged, and both grades
are kept (DECISIONS.md). The addendum also registered that a promoted sequence model runs in shadow
before it decides, because the API keeps no event history, so the live API still decides with
LightGBM.
{% endif %}
